  "recommended_range": [340000, 390000],
  "walk_away": 300000,
  "reasoning": "Demand of record (Nov. 2 letter): $428,399.50 = $265,200.00 deemed-accepted invoices + $11,499.50 accrued §2 interest (4,104.00+3,562.50+2,644.00+1,189.00) + $71,700.00 J-4533 (74,800.00 less our own $3,100.00 double-enter credit) + $80,000.00 conversion fees (5 hires, 25% x $64,000 placeholder, true-up to actual comp; Rosa/Tay waived in Bell's Feb. 11, 2026 writing and not claimed). §2 interest steps up +$2,652.00/month from Nov. 26-29 (684.00+712.50+661.00+594.50), so the figure is the same at a Nov. 17 filing as on Nov. 2 — no step-up lands before Nov. 26. Halvorsen & Price admitted the $265,200 in writing (Sept. 29: 'undisputed balance,' payable only on a conversion-fee condition found in no clause; §2 is unconditional). Probability-weighted value (counsel's judgment, arithmetic shown in strategy memo §5): 276,699.50 x 0.95 = 262,864.53; 71,700.00 x 0.60 = 43,020.00; 32,000.00 x 0.85 = 27,200.00; 48,000.00 x 0.50 = 24,000.00; EV = $357,084.53 gross of fees. File-vs-settle economics: EV minus assumed mid-case cost to take an award (47,500.00 attorney + 18,500.00 net AAA/arbitrator share = 66,000.00 [assumed — AAA fee schedule NOT IN LIBRARY — UNVERIFIED; pull at filing]) = 291,084.53 if no fee recovery; plus expected C.3 shift (0.7 x 0.75 recovery x 66,000.00 = 34,650.00) = 325,734.53; i.e., filing nets ~$290k–$330k over ~9–12 months [assumed timeline]. Hence: 340,000–390,000 beats filing on expected value and is the recommended landing band (consistent with strategy memo §5; supersedes Session 1's 274k–390k). walk_away = 300,000: between 300,000 and 340,000, accept only pre-filing, immediate cash, no interest holiday; below 300,000 a deal is dominated by filing, because the admitted core alone is ~0.95 certain, §2 interest keeps accruing during arbitration, and C.3 puts their fee exposure live once we are the claimant in the contractually required forum. Their Oct. 20, 2026 posture (call surfaced in Session 5 — pay 265,200.00 over 6 months, $0.00 on J-4533, $0.00 fees, mutual release, own fees) is REJECTED: it is 11,499.50 below the balance their own counsel admitted (accrued interest unpaid) and waives ~7,956.00 more §2 interest over the installment run (avg balance 132,600.00 x 1% x 6 = 7,956.00) — ~$19,455.50 less than the admitted number — in exchange for releases extinguishing ~$151,700.00 of live claims (71,700.00 J-4533 + 80,000.00 fees) plus our fee claim. Their C.3 threat on the call is directed at the tortious-interference count, which was abandoned on our own documents (§6 consequential bar; Ashby; Feb. 11 consent — advice §§5.3, 6; Rule 3.1) and will not appear in any pleading or settlement paper; that threat has no bite. Fee numbers in fee_exposure_if_arbitrated are worst-case tail, all components labeled assumed [not in library — unverified]; replace with the real AAA Commercial schedule at the Nov. 17 filing. Conditions and unresolved inputs (QUESTIONS.md Q11–Q14): pre-engagement letter authorship; Oct. 20 call recipient; actual per-hire compensation (true-up cuts both ways); their J-4533 audit findings due Nov. 16; our internal June shift-level inspection before filing.",
  "fee_exposure_if_arbitrated": 135000
}

